## Image Optimization (Mandatory)
```astro
---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import heroImage from '../assets/hero.png';
---

<!-- ✅ Correct — Astro optimizes automatically -->
<Image
  src={heroImage}
  alt="Description of image" 
  width={800}
  height={400}
  format="webp"
/>

<!-- ❌ Wrong — no optimization, no dimensions -->
<img src="/hero.png" />
```

Rules:
- Always use `<Image>` from `astro:assets` (not raw `<img>`) for local images
- Always specify `width` and `height` to prevent layout shift
- Use `format="webp"` for photographs
- Add meaningful `alt` text — never empty `alt=""` for meaningful images
- User-uploaded images (Supabase Storage): use Supabase image transform URL with size params

